# text_id = 1188
# text = One of the main charges that the commission laid at the Government in the Mesopotamia inquiry was that they were guilty of what it called in an elegant phrase , the misuse of reticence , or the culling of inconvenient facts to protect the official line — a practice that could as happily describe the Government 's Iraq policy today as it could the then Government 's policy 90 years ago .
