# text_id = 1233
# text = Like other hon . Members , I was a Member of Parliament in the 1990s when we voted on the prevention of terrorism Acts , and the notion that a short debate , late at night , with a whipped vote and all the media pressure to vote one way constitutes acceptable parliamentary scrutiny — not to mention the idea of our becoming some sort of grand jury — is laughable .
