# text_id = 1242
# text = When I raised a similar point on an earlier occasion , my right hon . Friend thought that there might be a possibility of appointing special counsel , such as those he is familiar with at the Special Immigration Appeals Commission , so that someone can represent the interests of the defendant in challenging that ex parte evidence without the obligation to report back to the defendant what he has heard .
