# text_id = 1278
# text = Given that the role of the courts which cannot be ousted is that of judicial review , and given that the period for applying for a judicial review is , I believe , six weeks rather than three months — which is the period mentioned in Amendment No. 39 — I should like to know how the provision fits within the context of the overall law of judicial review .
